    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d868">

                <pb facs="0826" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/835</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d868-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-14T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                                1917, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1899. Referring Department telegram 1890, December 8,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d868-f2"/> have approved following telegram sent by Ignatius,
                    Finnish Food Commissioner in United States, to Lars Krogius at Haparanda: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>State Department does not object to deputation coming here to state
                            Finland’s case but is not yet prepared to assume any position regarding
                            the recognition.</p></quote></p>
                <p>Advise Consul, Helsingfors.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d868-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d868-f1-content">
                <p>Similar telegram (No. 448) on the same date to the Minister in Sweden.</p>
            </note>
